The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (nft_set_elem_active(&rbe->ext, genmask)) {
    ...
    *ext = &rbe->ext;
    return -EEXIST;
}
```
Reason:
The condition checks if the existing element is active, and if so, it returns an error without progressing to the next branch. This leads to an endless loop when trying to re-insert an inactive element, as the logic does not correctly handle the transition from inactive to active states.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
else if (nft_set_elem_active(&rbe->ext, genmask)) {
    *ext = &rbe->ext;
    return -EEXIST;
} else {
    p = &parent->rb_left;
}
```
Reason:
The patch modifies the logic to ensure that the check for active elements is only performed after evaluating the conditions for interval ends. This allows the function to correctly select the next branch to inspect when re-inserting an inactive element, preventing the endless loop.

